# 1. Project Key Removal — Team Key as Sole Identifier

## Background

`ReportController.generateReport()` currently accepts a request object from the UI that includes a `projectKey` field. Project Key is a narrower concept than Team Key — one team can span multiple projects. Project Key should only ever be used internally for one purpose: fetching stories from iTrack. It should never be sent by the UI, stored as a primary identifier, or used to key any lookups outside that one iTrack call.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-1.1 | Remove `projectKey` from the Generate Report request DTO accepted by the UI. The UI must send only `teamKey` and `fixVersion`. |
| FR-1.2 | Anywhere `projectKey` is currently used to key logic, lookups, or responses (outside the iTrack story-fetch call), replace it with `teamKey`. |
| FR-1.3 | Where Project Key is genuinely required (the iTrack story-fetch call only), resolve it **server-side** from the Team Key via the team configuration YAML (`teamKey` → list of `projectKeys`) — never accept it as client input. |
| FR-1.4 | Remove `projectKey` from all response DTOs returned to the UI for Generate Report and related endpoints, unless the UI has an explicit, justified need to display it (default assumption: it does not). |
| FR-1.5 | Database-wide: remove `project_key` columns/references except where explicitly retained for iTrack-scoping purposes at the config/YAML level (not DB). See Section 12 for the specific `commits` table change. |
| FR-1.6 | Update any validation logic that currently checks `projectKey` presence to instead validate `teamKey` presence. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-1.1
GIVEN the UI submits a Generate Report request
WHEN the request payload is inspected
THEN it contains teamKey and fixVersion
AND it does NOT contain a projectKey field

AC-1.2
GIVEN a Generate Report request with a valid teamKey
WHEN the backend needs to fetch stories from iTrack
THEN it resolves the project key(s) internally from the team config YAML
AND does not require or accept a projectKey from the request

AC-1.3
GIVEN the codebase is searched for "projectKey" usage
WHEN results are reviewed
THEN the only remaining reference is the internal YAML-resolved value
used exclusively for the iTrack story-fetch call

AC-1.4
GIVEN a Generate Report response is returned to the UI
WHEN the payload is inspected
THEN no projectKey field is present unless explicitly required and justified

AC-1.5
GIVEN the request DTO validation runs
WHEN teamKey is missing
THEN a validation error is returned
AND projectKey is not part of the validation rules at all
```

