# 3. GitHub Call Optimization — Derive Head SHA from Prefetch Commits

## Background

During Generate Report, the prefetch commits step already fetches, in parallel per component, the full commit list for the release branch — ordered newest-first. Separately, the code makes an **additional GitHub API call per component** (`getBranchHeadSha()` or similarly named) purely to determine the head/latest commit SHA of that branch. This is redundant: the head commit is simply the first entry in the already-fetched, newest-first commit list.

## Problem Statement

An extra GitHub call per component, on top of the parallel prefetch, adds latency and unnecessary GitHub API rate-limit consumption at scale (100+ components).

## Required Change

```
BEFORE (redundant):

  Map<String, List<Commit>> prefetchedCommits =
      executorService.invokeAll(componentsFetchTasks);
      // parallel fetch, one GitHub call per component, newest-first ordering

  // ... later, separately:
  for (Component component : components) {
      String headSha = githubClient.getBranchHeadSha(
          component.getRepoUrl(), releaseBranch);
      // EXTRA GitHub call per component — redundant
  }


AFTER (optimized — single GitHub call batch, two outputs):

  Map<String, List<Commit>> prefetchedCommits =
      executorService.invokeAll(componentsFetchTasks);
      // UNCHANGED — same parallel fetch as before

  // Derive head SHA map from already-fetched data — NO extra GitHub call
  Map<String, String> headShaByComponent = prefetchedCommits.entrySet().stream()
      .collect(Collectors.toMap(
          Map.Entry::getKey,
          entry -> entry.getValue().isEmpty()
              ? null
              : entry.getValue().get(0).getSha()
              // first commit in newest-first list = head = latest commit
              // includes merge commits intentionally — this IS the head,
              // regardless of commit type
      ));
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-3.1 | Remove the separate per-component GitHub head-SHA call from the Generate Report flow. |
| FR-3.2 | Derive the head SHA for each component from the **first element** of its already-fetched, newest-first prefetch commits list. |
| FR-3.3 | The head SHA must include merge commits — do not filter merge commits out before taking the first element. This mirrors the existing rule established for the Deployment Section (Bundle 1 Section 5) — head/latest must always reflect the true latest commit. |
| FR-3.4 | If a component's prefetched commit list is empty, its head SHA must be `null` — do not throw an exception; log a WARN and continue processing other components. |
| FR-3.5 | The resulting head SHA map must be used to populate `components.release_branch_latest_commit_id` (established in Bundle 3 Section 10). |
| FR-3.6 | Total GitHub API calls for this step must not increase compared to the current prefetch-only call count — the head SHA extraction must add zero additional calls. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-3.1
GIVEN prefetch commits returns a newest-first ordered list for a component
WHEN the head SHA is derived
THEN it is exactly the SHA of the first (index 0) commit in that list
AND no additional GitHub API call is made to obtain it

AC-3.2
GIVEN the release branch's latest commit is a merge commit
WHEN the head SHA is derived
THEN the merge commit's SHA is used (not filtered out)

AC-3.3
GIVEN a component's prefetched commit list is empty
WHEN the head SHA is derived
THEN the value is null
AND a WARN is logged
AND processing continues for other components without failure

AC-3.4
GIVEN the optimization is implemented
WHEN GitHub API call counts are measured before and after for a 100-component run
THEN the call count is reduced by approximately 100 calls (one head-SHA call eliminated per component)
AND the prefetch commits call count is unchanged

AC-3.5
GIVEN the head SHA map is produced
WHEN components.release_branch_latest_commit_id is populated
THEN it uses this derived map — not a separate fetch
```

