# 4. Default Branch Name — Read from Team Config YAML

## Background

The code that fetches commits between the release branch and the main/master branch currently hardcodes the literal string `"master"` as the base branch. This will break for any team whose repositories use `"main"` as the default branch instead.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-4.1 | Add a `defaultBranch` field to the team configuration YAML, at the team level. |
| FR-4.2 | If `defaultBranch` is not specified for a team, fall back to `"master"` as the default value. |
| FR-4.3 | Remove the hardcoded `"master"` literal from the GitHub commit-comparison call sites. |
| FR-4.4 | All call sites that previously hardcoded `"master"` must instead read the resolved default branch for the relevant team. |
| FR-4.5 | Log the resolved default branch at DEBUG level whenever it is used in a GitHub call, for traceability. |

## YAML Configuration Example

```yaml
# team-config.yaml
teams:
  OC:
    teamKey: OC
    projectKeys: [SPT-OC]
    defaultBranch: master     # NEW — optional; defaults to "master" if omitted
    github:
      # ... existing config
    itrack:
      # ... existing config
```

## Code Change

```java
// BEFORE:
githubClient.getCommitsBetweenBranches(repoUrl, releaseBranch, "master");

// AFTER:
String defaultBranch = teamConfig.getDefaultBranch() != null
    ? teamConfig.getDefaultBranch()
    : "master"; // fallback default

githubClient.getCommitsBetweenBranches(repoUrl, releaseBranch, defaultBranch);
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-4.1
GIVEN team-config.yaml specifies defaultBranch: main for team "XYZ"
WHEN commits are fetched for that team
THEN "main" is used as the base branch — not "master"

AC-4.2
GIVEN team-config.yaml does NOT specify defaultBranch for team "OC"
WHEN commits are fetched for that team
THEN "master" is used as the fallback default

AC-4.3
GIVEN the codebase is searched for hardcoded "master" string literals
WHEN results are reviewed in the GitHub comparison call sites
THEN none remain — all resolve from team config

AC-4.4
GIVEN a GitHub call is made using the resolved default branch
WHEN DEBUG logging is enabled
THEN the resolved branch name is logged alongside the team key
```

