# 6. New Method — Prefetch Previous Release Branch & Main Branch Commits

## Background

A third commit-fetching method is required, distinct from the two that already exist:

1. **Prefetch commits** — the release branch's own commit history (used for head SHA, Section 3)
2. **Prefetch current branch & main commits** — current release branch vs. main/master (renamed in Section 5)
3. **NEW: Prefetch previous release branch & main commits** — main/master vs. the **previous** release branch

This third set captures commits that have landed on master/main but have not yet made it into the **previous** release branch — i.e., what has moved forward on master since the last release cut.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-6.1 | Create a new method, e.g., `prefetchPreviousReleaseBranchAndMainCommits()`. |
| FR-6.2 | Head branch = the resolved default branch (master/main, per Section 4 config). |
| FR-6.3 | Base branch = the component's **previous release branch** (already stored in `components.previous_branch`). |
| FR-6.4 | Execution must run **in parallel** across components, consistent with the existing prefetch patterns (ExecutorService). |
| FR-6.5 | Return type must match the existing prefetch pattern: `Map<String componentName, List<Commit>>`. |
| FR-6.6 | This method must be called during the same Generate Report phase as the other two prefetch steps, so all three commit sets are available before commit analysis begins. |

## Method Signature (Reference)

```java
/**
 * Fetches commits present on the default branch (master/main) that are
 * NOT yet present on each component's previous release branch.
 * Head branch: resolved default branch (from team config, Section 4)
 * Base branch: component.previousBranch
 */
Map<String, List<Commit>> prefetchPreviousReleaseBranchAndMainCommits(
        String teamKey,
        String fixVersion,
        List<Component> deployableComponents) {

    String defaultBranch = resolveDefaultBranch(teamKey);

    List<Callable<Map.Entry<String, List<Commit>>>> tasks =
        deployableComponents.stream()
            .map(component -> (Callable<Map.Entry<String, List<Commit>>>) () -> {
                List<Commit> commits = githubClient.getCommitsBetweenBranches(
                    component.getRepoUrl(),
                    defaultBranch,               // head
                    component.getPreviousBranch() // base
                );
                return Map.entry(component.getComponentName(), commits);
            })
            .collect(Collectors.toList());

    return executeInParallel(tasks); // reuse existing ExecutorService pattern
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-6.1
GIVEN a component with previousBranch = "release/26.06.14.rel"
AND resolved default branch = "master"
WHEN prefetchPreviousReleaseBranchAndMainCommits runs
THEN it fetches commits with head=master, base=release/26.06.14.rel

AC-6.2
GIVEN 50 deployable components
WHEN this new prefetch method runs
THEN all 50 component fetches execute in parallel via ExecutorService
AND total execution time is comparable to the existing prefetch steps (not sequential)

AC-6.3
GIVEN the three prefetch methods (commits, current+main, previous+main)
WHEN Generate Report executes
THEN all three complete before commit analysis (Section 13) begins

AC-6.4
GIVEN the new method follows the existing return type pattern
WHEN its output is inspected
THEN it returns Map<String, List<Commit>> keyed by component name,
consistent with the other two prefetch methods
```

