# 7. New Table — `commit_analysis_status`

## Background

During commit analysis, components are iterated and some are skipped from analysis (excluded, user-excluded, branch cut pending/missing, etc.). Currently, when a component is skipped, no record of that decision or reason is persisted — the information is lost. Additionally, when analysis IS performed, only in-memory/log data captures the resulting counts (compliant, non-compliant, reverted, cherry-picked, etc.) — nothing is durably stored per component.

## Problem Statement

There is no queryable, persistent record of commit analysis outcomes or skip reasons per component. This is needed both for auditability and to power a new UI tab (Section 8).

## Database Design

```sql
CREATE TABLE commit_analysis_status (
    id                            BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,

    -- Identity (composite key)
    team_key                      VARCHAR(50)  NOT NULL,
    fix_version                   VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    component_name                VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,

    -- Component Context (denormalized for direct UI display without extra joins)
    component_type                VARCHAR(50)  NULL,   -- SERVICE | LIBRARY | HELM | SYSTEM
    scrum_teams                   TEXT NULL,            -- JSON array, copied from components table
    stories                       TEXT NULL,            -- JSON array, copied from components table

    -- Analysis Execution State
    analysis_performed            BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    skip_reason                   VARCHAR(100) NULL,
        -- BRANCH_CUT_PENDING | BRANCH_CUT_MISSING | SYSTEM_EXCLUDED
        -- | USER_EXCLUDED | LIBRARY | OTHER

    -- Analysis Metrics (populated only when analysis_performed = TRUE)
    total_commits_analyzed        INT NULL,
    compliant_count                INT NULL,
    non_compliant_count            INT NULL,
    reverted_count                  INT NULL,
    cherry_picked_count             INT NULL,
    missing_cherry_pick_count       INT NULL,
    direct_release_commit_count     INT NULL,
    duplicate_commit_count          INT NULL,
    invalid_story_mapping_count     INT NULL,

    -- Overall Result
    overall_status                 VARCHAR(50) NULL,
        -- COMPLIANT | NON_COMPLIANT | PARTIAL | NOT_ANALYZED

    -- Timestamps (UTC)
    last_analyzed_at               TIMESTAMP NULL,

    -- Audit
    created_by                     VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    created_date                   TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_by                     VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    updated_date                   TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,

    CONSTRAINT uq_commit_analysis_status
        UNIQUE (team_key, fix_version, component_name)
);

-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_cas_team_fix
    ON commit_analysis_status(team_key, fix_version);

CREATE INDEX idx_cas_status
    ON commit_analysis_status(team_key, fix_version, overall_status);

CREATE INDEX idx_cas_skip_reason
    ON commit_analysis_status(team_key, fix_version, skip_reason);
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-7.1 | Create `commit_analysis_status` table with the schema above. |
| FR-7.2 | **Every** component for a given team + fix version must get a row — including Libraries, System Excluded, and User Excluded — not only components that undergo full analysis. |
| FR-7.3 | When a component is skipped from analysis, set `analysis_performed = FALSE` and populate `skip_reason` with the specific cause. |
| FR-7.4 | When analysis is performed, populate all metric columns and set `analysis_performed = TRUE`. |
| FR-7.5 | `scrum_teams` and `stories` must be copied from the `components` table at the time of analysis — this avoids a join when the UI tab (Section 8) loads. |
| FR-7.6 | This table must be **UPSERTed** — a re-run of Generate Report for the same team + fix version must update existing rows, not create duplicates (enforced by the unique constraint). |
| FR-7.7 | `overall_status` must be derived from the metric counts: `COMPLIANT` if `non_compliant_count = 0` and analysis was performed; `NON_COMPLIANT` if `non_compliant_count > 0`; `NOT_ANALYZED` if `analysis_performed = FALSE`. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-7.1
GIVEN Generate Report runs for team OC, fix version 26.7.4, with 80 components
WHEN commit analysis completes
THEN commit_analysis_status has exactly 80 rows for (OC, 26.7.4)
— one per component, regardless of whether analysis was performed or skipped

