# 15. TODO Comment Discipline — Scoped, Requirement-Matched Removal

## Background

This refines the general TODO audit approach from Bundle 4 Section 3, specifically for the requirements described in this document. Multiple TODO comments in the code correspond directly to items covered in this bundle. Some other TODOs relate to future work not being addressed now.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-15.1 | For each TODO comment in the code that corresponds to a requirement fully implemented in this bundle, **remove that specific TODO comment**. |
| FR-15.2 | For TODO comments that correspond to a requirement **partially** addressed in this bundle, remove only the portion of the TODO's content that has been completed; leave a clear, updated TODO describing what remains. |
| FR-15.3 | For TODO comments explicitly marked (per this session) as **not being worked on now** — deferred to a future step — leave the TODO **fully intact**, unchanged. |
| FR-15.4 | Do **not** perform a blanket removal of all TODOs — this is a precise, requirement-by-requirement matching exercise, not a general cleanup pass. |
| FR-15.5 | Where a TODO is removed, the surrounding code must reflect the completed implementation — a removed TODO with no corresponding code change is not acceptable. |

## Matching Guide

```
For each TODO found in scope:

  Does this TODO describe a requirement covered in Sections 1–14 above?
    NO  → Leave TODO untouched.
    YES → Continue:

      Is the requirement FULLY implemented as specified?
        YES → Remove the TODO comment entirely.
        NO (partial) → Update the TODO to describe only the remaining gap.
                        Remove the portion already completed.

      Was this specific TODO flagged in this session as
      "not being worked on right now / next steps"?
        YES → Leave TODO fully intact regardless of the above.
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-15.1
GIVEN a TODO comment describes "remove project key, use team key"
AND Section 1 of this bundle is fully implemented
WHEN the code is reviewed
THEN that specific TODO comment is removed

AC-15.2
GIVEN a TODO comment describes a requirement only partially completed in this bundle
WHEN the code is reviewed
THEN the TODO is updated to reflect only the remaining, unfinished portion

AC-15.3
GIVEN a TODO was explicitly flagged as deferred / not being worked on in this session
WHEN the code is reviewed
THEN that TODO remains fully intact, unmodified

AC-15.4
GIVEN the full set of TODOs in the affected files is reviewed
WHEN the matching guide is applied
THEN no TODO is removed without a corresponding, verifiable code change
implementing what it described
```

